  "title": "ftypes: implement is_nan for IEEE 11073 SFLOAT and FLOAT types",
  "description": "Summary:\n\nThe IEEE 11073 medical device floating-point type descriptors for FT_IEEE_11073_SFLOAT and FT_IEEE_11073_FLOAT previously had NULL is_nan function pointers with TODO markers.\n\nBecause ftype_can_is_nan() returned false for these types, the display filter semantic validator (fail_if_nan_cmp()) could not identify NaN or NRes (Not at this Resolution) special values, allowing invalid ordered comparison display filter expressions to pass semantic validation.\n\nChanges:\n\n\\- Implemented sfloat_ieee_11073_is_nan() and float_ieee_11073_is_nan() to detect NaN and NRes special values defined in ISO/IEEE 11073-20601.\n\n\\- Registered the functions in sfloat_type and float_type, resolving both TODO comments.",
