      "title": "ftypes: implement is_nan for IEEE 11073 SFLOAT and FLOAT types",
      "message": "ftypes: implement is_nan for IEEE 11073 SFLOAT and FLOAT types\n\nThe IEEE 11073 floating-point type handlers for FT_IEEE_11073_SFLOAT and FT_IEEE_11073_FLOAT had TODO comments with NULL is_nan function pointers in their ftype_t descriptors.\n\nConsequently, ftype_can_is_nan() returned false, preventing the display filter semantic checker (fail_if_nan_cmp()) from validating ordered comparisons against NaN and NRes special values.\n\nImplement sfloat_ieee_11073_is_nan() and float_ieee_11073_is_nan() to identify NaN and NRes special values in accordance with IEEE 11073-20601, and register them in their respective ftype_t tables.\n",
      "author_name": "Ayush Meel",
      "author_email": "ayushmeel.dev@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2026-09-11T18:06:25.000+05:30",
